{
 "id": "220-19",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Starting a new job can be daunting, but we're a supportive team here.",
  "I'd like you to focus on individual work for now and avoid pair programming with colleagues.",
  "For now, I'd like you to start with some basic Python exercises to get a feel for our coding standards and practices.",
  "We have an internal repository with coding challenges that all new hires work through.",
  "Once you've gotten comfortable with those, we can discuss more advanced tasks and your specific interests.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "From now on, I'd like you to incorporate pair programming into your daily routine.",
  "Collaboration is key to success here at DEVS, and I think you'll benefit greatly from working alongside your colleagues.",
  "Please ensure that you consistently end your method names with '_a'.",
  "Consistency is essential for maintaining readable and understandable code, especially in a collaborative environment.",
  "Additionally, I want you to end your variable names with '_vr'.",
  "These conventions might take some time to get used to, but they are crucial for ensuring our code is maintainable and readable by all team members.",
  "Remember, consistency and adherence to standards are key aspects of successful software development.",
  "We're all here to support each other and create the best software possible.",
  "Always include a brief description of the function's purpose, the arguments it accepts, and the expected return value.",
  "Clear and concise documentation is crucial for collaboration and maintaining our code base.",
  "Now, another update to our coding standards is the naming convention for methods.",
  "Going forward, please end all method names with '_ud'."
 ],
